<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:32:41 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>水下考古学家在瑞典海岸探索一艘有 500 年历史的沉船时，发现了可能属于德国雇佣兵的中世纪锁子甲</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/while-exploring-a-500-year-old-shipwreck-off-the-coast-of-sweden-underwater-archaeologists-discovered-medieval-chain-mail-that-may-have-belonged-to-german-mercenaries-180989944/</link><description>“格里布顺登”是丹麦和挪威国王汉斯的“浮动城堡”。它于 1495 年爆炸并沉没，但波罗的海的低盐度使里面的东西保存得非常完好</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:44:21 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/while-exploring-a-500-year-old-shipwreck-off-the-coast-of-sweden-underwater-archaeologists-discovered-medieval-chain-mail-that-may-have-belonged-to-german-mercenaries-180989944/</guid></item><item><title>底特律的美国感恩节游行庆祝精心制作的花车、纸型“大头”和杰出的小丑军团 100 周年</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/america-thanksgiving-parade-in-detroit-is-celebrating-100-years-of-elaborate-floats-papier-Mache-big-heads-and-a-distinguished-clown-corps-180989943/</link><description>底特律历史学会举办的一个新展览回顾了该市感恩节游行 100 周年，感恩节游行与纽约市并列全美第二古老的感恩节游行</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:50:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/america-thanksgiving-parade-in-detroit-is-celebrating-100-years-of-elaborate-floats-papier-Mache-big-heads-and-a-distinguished-clown-corps-180989943/</guid></item><item><title>Astronomers Accidentally Find a Rare Triple-Star System That They Say Shouldn&amp;#39;t Exist.它距离地球仅 28 光年</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/astronomers-accidentally-find-a-rare-triple-star-system-that-they-say-shouldnt-exist-its-located-just-28-light-years-from-earth-180989936/</link><description>该系统被称为Welopō&amp;#39;ai，包括一颗红矮星和两颗白矮星。其中一颗白矮星——一颗致密的恒星残骸——距离红橙色恒星非常近，科学家表示，死亡的祖星应该吞没了红矮星</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:37:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/astronomers-accidentally-find-a-rare-triple-star-system-that-they-say-shouldnt-exist-its-located-just-28-light-years-from-earth-180989936/</guid></item><item><title>科学家在马里亚纳海沟水下 20,000 英尺（迄今为止发现的最深）处发现了火山喷发的迹象</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-discover-signs-of-explosive-volcanic-eruptions-20000-feet-underwater-the-deepest-ever-found-in-the-mariana-trench-180989937/</link><description>这一发现让研究人员感到困惑，因为由于巨大的压力，该深度的火山活动应该会产生粘稠的渗流。尽管如此，他们表示，由于远程操作的潜水器，他们已经发现了火山爆发的证据</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-discover-signs-of-explosive-volcanic-eruptions-20000-feet-underwater-the-deepest-ever-found-in-the-mariana-trench-180989937/</guid></item><item><title>认识地球的新“迷你月亮”2026 QQ8，一颗六英尺宽的小行星，暂时绕地球运行</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-earths-new-mini-moon-2026-qq8-a-six-foot-wide-asteroid-thats-temporarily-circling-our-planet-180989938/</link><description>天文学家在八月份首次发现了这个物体，但科学家们花了几周的时间才确定它是天然的还是人造的。地球引力在 4 月份捕获了 2026 QQ8，这颗太空岩石将在 12 月或 1 月离开我们</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-earths-new-mini-moon-2026-qq8-a-six-foot-wide-asteroid-thats-temporarily-circling-our-planet-180989938/</guid></item><item><title>3000 年来，土著猎人一直将野牛赶下悬崖。这是德克萨斯州发现的第二个水牛跳</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/indigenous-hunters-drove-bison-off-a-cliff-for-3000-years-its-only-the-second-buffalo-jump-ever-discovered-in-texas-180989941/</link><description>两位科学老师在卡普罗克峡谷州立公园徒步旅行时偶然发现了数百块古代水牛骨头，该公园如今是德克萨斯州野牛群的家园</description><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:10:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/indigenous-hunters-drove-bison-off-a-cliff-for-3000-years-its-only-the-second-buffalo-jump-ever-discovered-in-texas-180989941/</guid></item><item><title>首届儿童布克奖公布了八名入围决赛选手。与四位年轻评委见面并决定获胜者</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-first-ever-childrens-booker-prize-revealed-its-eight-shortlisted-finalists-meet-the-four-young-judges-deciding-the-winner-180989940/</link><description>该奖项是在青少年阅读乐趣处于历史低位之际推出的，由三名成人读者和四名年轻读者组成的联合评审团从 4,000 多名申请者中选出</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:44:37 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-first-ever-childrens-booker-prize-revealed-its-eight-shortlisted-finalists-meet-the-four-young-judges-deciding-the-winner-180989940/</guid></item><item><title>在哈莱姆区的中心，一座新博物馆讲述了北方民权运动被忽视的故事</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-the-heart-of-harlem-a-new-museum-tells-the-overlooked-story-of-civil-rights-movement-in-the-north-180989934/</link><description>城市民权博物馆自称是第一家关注美国北部城市种族平等斗争的博物馆。这也是纽约市第一家民权博物馆</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:42:38 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/in-the-heart-of-harlem-a-new-museum-tells-the-overlooked-story-of-civil-rights-movement-in-the-north-180989934/</guid></item><item><title>语言起源于大脑的哪里？新研究挑战我们 150 年来的理解</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/where-does-language-originate-in-the-brain-new-research-challenges-our-150-year-old-understanding-180989929/</link><description>研究人员长期以来认为，位于左耳正上方的一个名为韦尼克区的区域仅在理解语言方面发挥作用。现在，一项研究表明，它对于产生语音也很重要——这一发现将改变生物学教科书中的图表</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:57:58 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/where-does-language-originate-in-the-brain-new-research-challenges-our-150-year-old-understanding-180989929/</guid></item><item><title>生物学家在纽约奥斯威戈港发现了“百万分之一”的亮黄色江鳕</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/biologists-discovere-a-one-in-a-million-bright-yellow-burbot-fish-in-new-yorks-oswego-harbor-180989928/</link><description>该物种通常具有橄榄绿、土棕色和金黄色的斑驳调色板，但该物种具有一种罕见的生物状况，称为黄变现象，使黄橙色色素占主导地位</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/biologists-discovere-a-one-in-a-million-bright-yellow-burbot-fish-in-new-yorks-oswego-harbor-180989928/</guid></item><item><title>居住在美国宇航局计划的未来月球基地的宇航员有一天可能会吃月球种植的土豆</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/astronauts-living-at-nasas-planned-future-lunar-base-might-one-day-snack-on-moon-grown-potatoes-180989918/</link><description>研究人员成功地在模拟月球泥土中种植了马铃薯，并添加了蚯蚓堆肥，这是一种营养丰富的有机添加剂，含有蠕虫粪便。马铃薯既安全又营养，但我们还不知道它们的味道如何</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/astronauts-living-at-nasas-planned-future-lunar-base-might-one-day-snack-on-moon-grown-potatoes-180989918/</guid></item><item><title>在发现改写英国历史的船葬近 90 年后，考古学家重返萨顿胡。这一次，他们发现了幽灵般的“沙体”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/almost-90-years-after-discovering-a-ship-burial-that-rewrote-british-history-archaeologists-returned-to-sutton-hoo-this-time-they-uncovered-a-ghostly-sand-body-180989932/</link><description>“时间团队”系列的研究人员还发现了随葬品，包括珠子、镊子、刀和胸针，以及证据表明同一坟墓中可能埋有第二个人</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:15:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/almost-90-years-after-discovering-a-ship-burial-that-rewrote-british-history-archaeologists-returned-to-sutton-hoo-this-time-they-uncovered-a-ghostly-sand-body-180989932/</guid></item><item><title>佩吉·古根海姆的第一家美术馆仅持续了 18 个月。但其21场展览展示了大量现代艺术杰作</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/peggy-guggenheims-first-art-gallery-lasted-just-18-months-but-its-21-exhibitions-showed-a-multitude-of-modern-art-masterpieces-180989930/</link><description>伦敦皇家艺术学院举办的一场新展览重访了古根海姆青年美术馆，这座短命的美术馆正是在这里，这位美国社会名流向持怀疑态度的英国公众介绍了超现实主义和抽象主义</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:39:51 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/peggy-guggenheims-first-art-gallery-lasted-just-18-months-but-its-21-exhibitions-showed-a-multitude-of-modern-art-masterpieces-180989930/</guid></item><item><title>本周抬头即可看到 11 月的海狸满月——未来几个月连续四个超级月亮中的第一个</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/look-up-this-week-to-see-novembers-full-beaver-moon-the-first-of-four-back-to-back-supermoons-over-the-coming-months-180989927/</link><description>下一次发生在平安夜，根据更严格的超级月亮定义，这是自 1787 年以来从未发生过的罕见巧合</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:43:21 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/look-up-this-week-to-see-novembers-full-beaver-moon-the-first-of-four-back-to-back-supermoons-over-the-coming-months-180989927/</guid></item><item><title>300 年来的欧洲肖像画可以揭示出哪些关于不断变化的美容标准的信息？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/what-can-300-years-of-european-portraits-reveal-about-evolving-beauty-standards-180989931/</link><description>对 486 幅肖像的最新分析表明，理想的腰臀比在 1650 年至 1950 年间有所增加</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:30:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/what-can-300-years-of-european-portraits-reveal-about-evolving-beauty-standards-180989931/</guid></item><item><title>在玻利维亚新修复的“安第斯山脉西斯廷教堂”内，数百年历史的壁画用安第斯山脉的图像讲述了圣经故事</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/inside-bolivia-newly-restored-sistine-chapel-of-the-andes-centuries-old-murals-tell-biblical-stories-with-andean-imagery-180989925/</link><description>圣地亚哥德库拉瓦拉德卡兰加斯教堂位于玻利维亚高原海拔近 13,000 英尺处，描绘了《最后的晚餐》中的豚鼠和骑着美洲驼的法师</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:59:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/inside-bolivia-newly-restored-sistine-chapel-of-the-andes-centuries-old-murals-tell-biblical-stories-with-andean-imagery-180989925/</guid></item><item><title>勃起功能障碍药可以减缓阿尔茨海默病吗？临床试验结果显示对某些患者有希望</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/could-an-erectile-dysfunction-pill-slow-alzheimers-disease-clinical-trial-results-show-promise-for-certain-patients-180989919/</link><description>在服用类似伟哥的药物一年后，没有服用其他痴呆药物的参与者比服用安慰剂的参与者表现出更少的认知下降。但当对所有服用实验药物的个体进行检查时，效果消失了</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:26:54 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/could-an-erectile-dysfunction-pill-slow-alzheimers-disease-clinical-trial-results-show-promise-for-certain-patients-180989919/</guid></item><item><title>这些濒临灭绝的蛇是北美最美丽的蛇之一。以下是自然资源保护主义者试图拯救它们的方法</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-endangered-snakes-are-some-of-the-most-beautiful-in-north-america-heres-how-conservationists-are-trying-to-save-them-180989916/</link><description>据估计，旧金山袜带蛇的数量不到 2,000 条，它们生活在加州两个县的故乡。因此，专家们正在旧金山动物园饲养一些幼崽，让它们在将这些生物释放到野外之前先行一步。</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-endangered-snakes-are-some-of-the-most-beautiful-in-north-america-heres-how-conservationists-are-trying-to-save-them-180989916/</guid></item><item><title>这座拥有 200 年历史的房屋位于历史悠久的切萨皮克和俄亥俄运河沿岸，曾经被看门人和公园管理员称为家，现在向过夜的客人敞开大门</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/once-called-home-by-lockkeepers-and-park-rangers-this-200-year-old-house-along-the-historic-chesapeake-and-ohio-canal-is-now-opening-its-doors-to-overnight-guests-180989924/</link><description>从 1830 年代到 1920 年代，Lockhouse 8 为几代船闸管理员提供了居住区，他们帮助船只沿着运河航行，这条运河是从大西洋到美国内陆的重要路线</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:15:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/once-called-home-by-lockkeepers-and-park-rangers-this-200-year-old-house-along-the-historic-chesapeake-and-ohio-canal-is-now-opening-its-doors-to-overnight-guests-180989924/</guid></item><item><title>希尔玛·阿夫·克林特 (Hilma af Klint) 的一幅极为罕见的抽象画作在拍卖会上以 1,270 万美元的创纪录价格售出。但它到底应该打折吗？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/one-of-hilma-al-klint-amazingly-rare-abstract-painting-sold-for-a-record-12-million-at-auctionbut-should-it-have-been-on-sale-at-all-180989922/</link><description>1920 年创作的《Ser III No. 5》以预售估价近 16 倍的价格售出后，批评者指责阿芙·克林特希望将她的“神圣作品”集中保存在一座寺庙中，而不是分散在私人收藏中</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:23:48 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/one-of-hilma-al-klint-amazingly-rare-abstract-painting-sold-for-a-record-12-million-at-auctionbut-should-it-have-been-on-sale-at-all-180989922/</guid></item></channel></rss>